# Theme System

## Architecture

```
ThemePalette (TypeScript)     →  CSS Variables  →  Tailwind Classes
  orange-warm.ts / blue-cold.ts    engine.ts          tailwind.config.ts
                                   applyTheme()       colorVar("bg")
```

One palette = a `ThemePalette` object with two token sets: `light` + `dark`.
`applyTheme()` sets CSS variables on `<html>`.
Tailwind reads them via `var(--color-*)`.

## Creating a New Palette

1. Create a file `shared/lib/themes/my-palette.ts`:

```typescript
import type { ThemePalette } from "./tokens";

export const myPalette: ThemePalette = {
  id: "my-palette",
  name: "My Palette",
  dark: {
    bg: "#...",
    "bg-elevated": "#...",
    // ... all 42 tokens from PaletteTokens
  },
  light: {
    bg: "#...",
    // ... all 42 tokens
  },
};
```

2. Register in `shared/lib/themes/registry.ts`:

```typescript
import { myPalette } from "./my-palette";
export const palettes = [orangeWarm, blueCold, myPalette];
```

Done — the palette is available in the UI.

## Token Groups (42 tokens)

| Group | Tokens | Tailwind |
|-------|--------|---------|
| Surfaces | `bg`, `bg-elevated`, `card-bg`, `card-bg-active`, `text-field-bg` | `bg-bg`, `bg-card-bg` |
| Typography | `text-primary`, `text-secondary`, `text-muted` | `text-text-primary` |
| Brand | `accent`, `accent-soft`, `on-accent` | `bg-accent`, `text-on-accent` |
| Borders | `border-subtle` | `border-border-subtle` |
| Sidebar | `sidebar-bg`, `sidebar-item-hover`, `sidebar-sender`, `sidebar-unread` | `bg-sidebar-bg` |
| Composer | `composer-outer`, `composer-send`, `composer-icon` | `bg-composer-send` |
| Messages | `msg-bg`, `msg-own-bg`, `msg-time`, `msg-call-bg`, `msg-selected` | `bg-msg-own-bg` |
| Icons | `icon-base`, `icon-disable`, `icon-hover`, `icon-active` | `text-icon-base` |
| Notice | `notice-base`, `notice-disable`, `badge-bg`, `badge-text` | `bg-badge-bg` |
| Call | `call-bg`, `call-green` | `bg-call-bg` |
| Search | `search-bg`, `search-hint` | `bg-search-bg` |
| Indicators | `indicator-yellow`, `-pink`, `-purple`, `-green`, `-orange` | `bg-indicator-green` |

## Store API

```typescript
import { useThemeStore } from "~/entities/theme";

const { paletteId, mode, setPalette, setMode, toggleMode } = useThemeStore();

setPalette("blue-cold");     // Switch palette
setMode("light");            // Switch mode
setMode("system");           // Follow OS preference
toggleMode();                // Dark ↔ Light
```

## Rules

- NEVER use hardcoded colors in components (`bg-[#333]` is forbidden)
- Always use semantic tokens: `bg-bg`, `text-text-primary`, `bg-accent`
- If a new token is needed — add to `PaletteTokens` interface + all palettes + Tailwind config
- CSS fallbacks in `index.css` = Orange Warm Dark (for the first render before JS initializes)
